  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly admits photo limitations, screens for major infection/warning signs (RC3 met), gives a stratified emergency vs. routine follow-up path (RC4 met), prohibits self-directed antibiotic changes (RC5 met), clarifies the distinction between topical repair agents and systemic antibiotics (RC6 met), provides safe re-photography/observation guidance without forced dressing removal (RC7 met), and obtains actionable receipts (RC9 met). No serious chain error occurs. One minor deficiency affects RC1: the doctor uses slightly overconfident language that ‘the combination of current findings does not seem like a systemic infection’ without systematically reaffirming that the photo itself cannot rule out local infection; this makes RC1 a minor error. Consequently the maximum grade is 2 (Borderline). Two high-order points (HO1, HO3) are partially demonstrated but not fully completed with distinct beyond-minimum evidence, and the HO1 evidence overlaps with RC-chain duties, so they cannot lift the grade above the RC cap.",
